From 1aec44898dc9c913ee9adb88d868f1ba9a9c8a58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:50:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/57] hw/char: SERCOM SPI host and I2C host, checked against
 PIC32CM MC00

SPI host (MODE 3): each DATA write shifts out on the SERCOM's SSI bus
and the reply goes into the two-character receive buffer; an input pad
on the output pad loops back, an unconnected input reads 0xFF; a lost
character shows as STATUS.BUFOVF/INTFLAG.ERROR and a 0 in its place when
the buffer runs empty (silicon).

I2C host (MODE 5): ADDR starts a transfer on the SERCOM's I2C bus (MB,
or SB with the first byte), DATA writes and smart-mode reads, CTRLB.CMD
repeated start, byte read and stop; STATUS.BUSSTATE UNKNOWN after
enable, IDLE when forced, OWNER during a transfer and briefly after the
stop; CLKHOLD and RXNACK as seen on silicon.

MC00 board: the EDBG data gateway, the only device on the board's I2C
bus (the ATECC608A footprint is not fitted), acknowledges at 0x28, reads
0x00 and ignores the general call. New qtests for both modes.

Peripheral Pretender: a personal project; not for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
